Surface: com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/MetricCard (MetricCard.kt view + MetricCardModel.kt pure model) ports web
components/data-display/MetricCard.tsx: a compact metric tile (label + value[string|number] + neon accent icon box +
subtitle + inline HelpTooltip + a mutually-exclusive legacy change pill / direction-aware delta). It is purely
presentational (no async feed of its own), so -- like the accepted VisuallyHidden / AnimatedNumber / Delta ports -- no
error/stale/offline lifecycle is fabricated; its real branches are the base value, +subtitle, +help, +icon/accent, the
change-pill footer, and the delta footer. The delta footer delegates to the SHIPPED
io.teslasync.android.sharedsurfaces.delta.Delta surface (the P1/S8 settings-bound version), so the user's unit
preferences flow through the shared settings state holder; no direct HTTP from the view.
Neon accent (web NeonColor) -> theme tokens, never a raw hex: cyan->status.info, green->status.success,
red->status.danger, amber->status.warning, purple->chart.power, blue->chart.speed.
i18n: the only key the card owns is the help trigger label -> translation_help_tooltip_iconLabel (web
help.tooltip.iconLabel), resolved through the P1/S10 catalog; no English literal lives in native code.
Telemetry: view.opened slug=MetricCard (P1/S11), recorded once per surface open, PII-safe (slug only).
a11y: the help trigger carries a localized contentDescription; the accent icon is decorative unless named; label and
value are real text nodes.

androidTest (UI/a11y): MetricCardUiTest.kt authored -- 7 cases (label+value, subtitle, localized help a11y label,
positive/negative change pill, delta-slot routing, named accent icon) -- mirroring the accepted DeltaUiTest. It executes
under :android:connectedAndroidTest on a device/emulator (no device on this runner), the same split the sibling Delta /
BatteryDelta surfaces document; the offline gate's testReleaseUnitTest covers the pure model. MetricCardUiTest.kt has
